{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Sibling sweep (Step 7) — construct and parity axes\n\n**Construct: \"a proxied nginx location with no explicit `proxy_read_timeout`.\"** Two other\nlocations in `rebar.conf.template` share it — `/review/` and `/opcert/`. Both were checked against\nthe host's nginx logs rather than changed on suspicion.\n\n**Parity census of every 504 nginx has served (full retained access log):**\n\n```\n  32  Gerrit git  (git-upload-pack / info/refs)   <- this bug\n ~11  Gerrit REST (/a/changes/...)                <- SAME location block; also fixed\n   2  /mcp                                        <- has an explicit 3600s; different cause\n   0  /review/\n   0  /opcert/\n```\n\nTwo useful consequences:\n\n1. **The fix's blast radius is wider than the reported symptom, and correctly so.** The Gerrit\n   REST 504s (`/a/changes/<n>/detail?o=LABELS`, the change-status polls the voter and tooling\n   make) and the Gerrit UI's static assets (`/elements/gr-app.js` 237 upstream timeouts,\n   `/fonts/material-icons.woff2` 207) sit in the *same* `location /` block and were failing for\n   the *same* reason. One directive covers all of them. This is very likely a contributor to the\n   `voter_errors` climb noted on `ergophobic-harassed-peacock`.\n\n2. **`/review/` and `/opcert/` are NOT confirmed siblings — no speculative change made.**\n   `/review/health` does show 254 upstream-timeout lines in the error log, but produced **zero**\n   504s, so those are a different class (connect-side, most likely the container being down across\n   a redeploy) and belong to `erratic-sunny-genet` / review-bot ops rather than here. `/opcert/`\n   shows nothing at all. Neither has a measured duration distribution that would justify a value,\n   and inventing one would be the plausibility-driven fix this investigation exists to avoid.\n   **Disposition: left unchanged, recorded here.**\n\n3. **`/mcp`'s 2 504s are not this construct** — it already carries an explicit `3600s`, so a\n   missing timeout cannot be the cause. That is `witted-invisible-roan` (`9ea3-7d07`), separately\n   tracked.\n\n**Push path is covered too.** One of the timeouts was\n`GET /a/rebar/info/refs?service=git-receive-pack` — a *push's* ref advertisement. It is a response\nread, so it sits under the same `proxy_read_timeout` and is fixed by the same directive.\n`proxy_send_timeout` (request-body upload, the other half of a push) is still on its 60s default;\nno evidence of it firing was found, so it is left alone rather than changed pre-emptively."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788649268584327001,"uuid":"771a2f09-cc9a-4ae3-8433-442ba3505408"}